{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here","id":1472681,"title":"Lore of Traditions is here","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-18T10:55:42-08:00","id":1472681,"title":"Lore of Traditions is here","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/339646881/lore-of-the-traditions-for-the-mage-20th-anniversary-ttrpg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Everybody has a secret world inside of them. All of the people of the world, I mean everybody. No matter how dull and boring they are on the outside, inside them they\u2019ve all got unimaginable, magnificent, wonderful, stupid, amazing worlds. Not just one world. Hundreds of them. Thousands maybe.&quot;</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T15:02:34-08:00","id":1472697,"title":"","content":"I was fourth to pledge. The campaign was funded in 62 minutes, and hit its first stretch goal a little over an hour later. As I write this (less than an hour after the first stretch goal was hit, and about three hours into the campaign), we're about $250 away from the second stretch goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T00:26:23-08:00","id":1472756,"title":"","content":"Let's hope that its success also leads to a book about the disparates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T02:19:54-08:00","id":1472761,"title":"","content":"The Stretch Goal that was just unlocked a few hours ago was: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><u>Forgotten Ones and Forbidden Orders</u><br /> A collection of lesser known but no less magickally potent orders, traditions, cults, and gatherings of mages, from the Ahl-i-Batin to Ngoma (<i>and some in between</i>) will be created and released as a small M20 PDF Supplement. All Kickstarter backers receiving the <b>M20 Lore of the Traditions PDF</b> will automatically have this PDF added to their reward list.</div>Basically, the beginnings of a Lore of the Disparates/M20 Book of Crafts has just been achieved; I expect that later Stretch Goals will include some that increase the page count and scope of this. In fact, that's confirmed a bit later in the same Update that announced the Stretch Goal: <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">With these, we'll have established our two primary Stretch Goal projects - <b>Faces of Magick</b> and <b>Forgotten Ones &amp; Forbidden Orders</b>. Let's see if we can initiate both of these projects and then get to work expanding them both, with a few more fun stops along the way!</div><br /> And note that we hit this goal about 12 hours in, barely half a day into the full 30-day run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T05:57:14-08:00","id":1472767,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Just out of curiosity, is there any supplement any of you would like to see as a stretch goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T06:22:36-08:00","id":1472769,"title":"","content":"They've already established that they'll be providing two: Faces of Magick, which is a Who's Who of the Traditions; and Forgotten Ones &amp; Forbidden Orders, which looks like it's going to be the Disparates. I don't expect that we'll be getting any more. <br /> <br /> But my wish list would be an M20 Book of Madness. It's now the only \u201cfaction\u201d without a book (or the promise of one) in M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T08:17:00-08:00","id":1472780,"title":"","content":"What's the stance on sharing content from the manuscripts for discussion? Is there a specific limit, or should one refrain from quoting any text and discussing the content more abstractly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T08:29:46-08:00","id":1472781,"title":"","content":"From past experience, use \u201cfair use\u201d guidelines. I've had no problem in the past with quoting those parts of the text that are directly relevant to what's being discussed; but doing an infodump of whole sections of a chapter (let alone whole chapters) is a no-no. <br /> <br /> Put another way, you can be fairly confident that Onyx Path won't have a problem with you if your post effectively doubles as free advertising for them (whetting people's appetites and making them want to back it); but they <i>will</i> have a problem if your post <i>discourages</i> people from considering backing it (\u201cwhy should I bother backing it when this guy has given me all of the text already, for free?\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T08:36:06-08:00","id":1472783,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice, I'll try to act judiciously in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T07:12:42-08:00","id":1472963,"title":"","content":"I hope they will include some sorcerer groups in the Forgotten Ones book or just a chapter talking about sorcerers among the traditions. But that seems unlikely, though I could still ask in the comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T07:24:44-08:00","id":1472965,"title":"","content":"Two of the Potential Recruits for the Disparate Alliance were originally introduced as sorcerer factions. Given that there's no <i>official</i> S20 book, I think it's a near-certainty that they'll be reinvented as mage factions if they end up getting included. That <i>does</i> potentially open the door for other sorcerer factions to similarly be reinvented and included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T08:54:28-08:00","id":1473075,"title":"","content":"Sahajya Preview!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T15:51:20-08:00","id":1473213,"title":"","content":"Backed for Deluxe (basically my knee jerk response to being offered literally any official mage supplement). That said, I subsequently listened to the most recent Mage The Podcast episode where they interviewed some of upcoming book's authors, and, I'm <i>tempering </i>my expectations a little at this point. The interview seemed to focus more on what the authors are doing to correct nomenclature, and culturally insensitive material from past editions, than on new or updated factions, intrigues and politics, the evolution of any given paradigm for 2021, etc. Don't get me wrong, I think these kinds of changes are important to modernizing the game as a whole, and bringing in new players who don't have the rose-colored nostalgia glasses to rationalize the cringier stuff (and frankly, the less cringe in the game, the better,) but the day the review copy gets released to backers, the content (if present) that's going to get me so jazzed that I end up losing a day's worth of work reading the PDF in my office because I can't wait to get home <i>won't be</i> the sociopolitically conscientious errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T18:42:00-08:00","id":1473307,"title":"","content":"the full Sahajiya chapter is here,it takes a good hard look at the Tradition warts and all,and i love it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T20:48:16-08:00","id":1473311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473213#post1473213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backed for Deluxe (basically my knee jerk response to being offered literally any official mage supplement). That said, I subsequently listened to the most recent Mage The Podcast episode where they interviewed some of upcoming book's authors, and, I'm <i>tempering </i>my expectations a little at this point. The interview seemed to focus more on what the authors are doing to correct nomenclature, and culturally insensitive material from past editions, than on new or updated factions, intrigues and politics, the evolution of any given paradigm for 2021, etc. Don't get me wrong, I think these kinds of changes are important to modernizing the game as a whole, and bringing in new players who don't have the rose-colored nostalgia glasses to rationalize the cringier stuff (and frankly, the less cringe in the game, the better,) but the day the review copy gets released to backers, the content (if present) that's going to get me so jazzed that I end up losing a day's worth of work reading the PDF in my office because I can't wait to get home <i>won't be</i> the sociopolitically conscientious errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry too much about it. I've read the chapters released thus far; and what the writers focus on talking about during an interview doesn't really align with how they allot word count in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T13:17:06-08:00","id":1473423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473311#post1473311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't worry too much about it. I've read the chapters released thus far; and what the writers focus on talking about during an interview doesn't really align with how they allot word count in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good to know! I guess I'll prepare to lose that entire day of work after all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T13:56:35-08:00","id":1473424,"title":"","content":"Are you guys liking it so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T14:07:35-08:00","id":1473425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473424#post1473424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you guys liking it so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>The writing is great and the additions for each Traditions are flavorful. I was hoping that each chapter would be as parallel in structure as V20's Lore of Clans. Not every Tradition gets new Rotes, some get new Foci, and others have gotten items. I personally wanted Rotes, Merits, and Flaws for each Tradition, but I also understand that M20 is a different beast than V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T15:45:45-08:00","id":1473431,"title":"","content":"I rather like what I've read so far. The most \u201cdisappointing\u201d chapter thus far has been the Celestial Chorus; though I'm still having some trouble putting my finger on just what it is about that chapter that's bugging me. But even there, what I know is that it has less to do with what is being said and more to do with <i>how</i> is being said: once I read it three or four times to puzzle out the \u201cwhat\u201d, I found myself agreeing with it. <br /> <br /> And the other chapters? Hardly any problems at all. My only overall complaint is that they didn't have the page count to go into each Tradition's Factions; I'm hoping that we'll eventually get a stretch goal that either increases the word count to include Faction write-ups or funds a series of PDF supplements to that effect. <br /> <br /> On the plus side, I really like that the Celestial Chorus is getting a counterpart to the Syndicate's Ventures, but based on religious communities instead of business enterprises. The Akashayana and Sahajira (\u201cCult of Ecstasy\u201d) aren't adding anything new, mechanics-wise; but they're definitely giving me a much clearer understanding of those Traditions. <br /> <br /> And yeah; M20 is very definitely a different beast than V20. One of the key differences is that M20 is big on the idea that all views have something significant to contribute, and that each should be considered on its own terms. This is reinforced by the fact that the various Tradition chapters are so wildly different from each other and don't follow a cookie cutter formula. <br /> <br /> That said, if you want a book of Merits and Flaws for each Tradition, let me point you to <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/376608\" target=\"_blank\">Hermetic Hipsters Guide to the Traditions</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-27-2022, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T07:24:23-08:00","id":1473463,"title":"","content":"Without going into details, are the Chorus still largely a secret and ancient conspiracy of monist/theosophist/gnostics or are they getting more of the ecumenical defense pact treatment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T07:50:27-08:00","id":1473465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473463#post1473463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without going into details, are the Chorus still largely a secret and ancient conspiracy of monist/theosophist/gnostics or are they getting more of the ecumenical defense pact treatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first one; they're not being given an overhaul here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T08:25:17-08:00","id":1473466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473463#post1473463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without going into details, are the Chorus still largely a secret and ancient conspiracy of monist/theosophist/gnostics or are they getting more of the ecumenical defense pact treatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re not going to rewrite the existing history for the most part, but there is definitely more focus on the ecumenical diversity now, with the Christian Septarians largely having walked for the Knights Templar over the current leadership\u2019s reforms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T09:56:51-08:00","id":1473473,"title":"","content":"As it was mentioned, my only issue is that there's no mention to the factions of each tradition. I really hope they get a chance to expand on it with a stretch goal. Apart from that, I'm loving it. I used to see the traditions as passive organizations that only reacted to events to ensure their survival. This book gives them nuance, personality and most important a clear objective beyond simple survival. For the first time since forever, I want to run a campaign with tradition mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 01-28-2022, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T10:16:29-08:00","id":1473475,"title":"","content":"One more reason why I'd really like to see them include the various Traditions' Factions in one way or another is that, as glamour weaver pointed out, a bunch of Choristers walked and joined the Templars. The effects of this are detailed ina section entitled \u201cThe Loss of the Guardian Orders\u201d. <br /> <br /> There's also a paragraph at the start of Current Issues that goes like this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The Chorus's score experienced more revisions in the previous 20 years than in the prior five centuries. The Chorus forges itself anew and is finding not every Singer has found a new home among its sections. </div>The history of the Chorus remains the same, with recent additions; but the <i>nature</i> of the Chorus has radically shifted. Given that, we really need a look at the new status of the Chorister Factions.<br /> <br /> I'm reading through the Kha'vadi as I write this; and the Dreamspeakers are another Tradition desperately in need of updated Factions: both the Four Winds and the Solitaries were devastated by the Avatar Storm; the former flat out ceased to exist, and the latter has been decimated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-28-2022, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:24:40-08:00","id":1473489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473466#post1473466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They\u2019re not going to rewrite the existing history for the most part, but there is definitely more focus on the ecumenical diversity now, with the Christian Septarians largely having walked for the Knights Templar over the current leadership\u2019s reforms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes it sound like they have less ecumenical diversity, not more. If the factions that value their specific religious beliefs over the &quot;secret true monotheism&quot; are leaving that means the latter make up a much bigger part of the Tradition.<br /> <br /> That said, I should probably read the section rather than ask for details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:41:31-08:00","id":1473491,"title":"","content":"As with the write-up that's presented in M20, the Celestial Chorus is now focused less on individual religious dogmas and more on broad, shared principles. The whole thing is centered around the Five Doctrines: the Doctrine of Charity (we have limited resources, and must direct them to where they'll do the most good), the Doctrine of Comity (ignore doctrines that break harmony), the Doctrine of Compassion (act with compassion and love toward the Sleepers, not scorn), the Doctrine of Foresight (plan ahead!), and the Doctrine of Harmony (seek out the voices that have been hushed or ignored). <br /> <br /> Comity, in particular, is why the Guardian Orders left for the Templars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T17:31:00-08:00","id":1473507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473489#post1473489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That makes it sound like they have less ecumenical diversity, not more. If the factions that value their specific religious beliefs over the &quot;secret true monotheism&quot; are leaving that means the latter make up a much bigger part of the Tradition.<br /> <br /> That said, I should probably read the section rather than ask for details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not that the remaining groups necessarily are those that value secret Monism, but they are those who can embrace the Chorus\u2019 diversity of religious beliefs. The ones who are gone are those who effectively got Paradox of Toleranced out the door (technically they walked but because of policies that were obviously going to alienate them),<br /> <br /> that said, it may be worth noting in the errata that this seems to only account for the burn the heretic Christian sects, as they join the Templars. But obviously any Muslim or Hindu Chorister etc hardline septarian didn\u2019t go Templar, so where are they? New Crafts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-28-2022, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T18:35:56-08:00","id":1473512,"title":"","content":"The Batini might have a place for some of them. That said, it's stated that many of them went to other Traditions, or just went solo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T13:59:49-08:00","id":1473593,"title":"","content":"You know what I want to see? I want to see the Order of Hermes that the rest of the Council <i>wants</i> to align with. I want the Order that contributes something <i>unique and useful</i>, the one that the other traditions may not <i>like</i>, but <i>respect and trust</i> enough to ally with. I want to see members of the Order of Hermes that aren't insufferable ignorant prigs, or apologetic about the Order of Hermes' past before anything, but ones who agree with the Order of Hermes' way of doing things, and maybe had their lives improved by their association with the Hermetic philosophy. <br /> <br /> I'm tired of them being the constant assholes. I want to play a Hermetic without the constant reminder that these guys were all shitbags. Just one incarnation where they had something <i>redeeming</i> to them, before I die or grow out of the hobby. The author interview gave me a few moments of hope, but I'd like to see a more positive direction for the Hermetics going forward. <br /> <br /> Rant over. Thank you for coming to my TED-Talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T14:13:16-08:00","id":1473594,"title":"","content":"I have mixed views on this. Not on what I <i>want</i> to see, mind you; I'm entirely with you on that. No; the past where I'm conflicted it's that while the latest interview <i>does</i> provide some reason for hope, the first interview had the guy in charge saying that one of his bits of advice for the authors was \u201cblame the Hermetics\u201d when problematic material came up. I'd much rather they <i>don't</i> try to dump everything on the Hermetics, for the same reason I prefer that the Technocracy owns its own failings and doesn't foist then off on the Nephandi. In both cases, I'm not a big fan of scapegoating. Own up to your own problems, and then move forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T16:52:55-08:00","id":1473607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473594#post1473594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mixed views on this. Not on what I <i>want</i> to see, mind you; I'm entirely with you on that. No; the past where I'm conflicted it's that while the latest interview <i>does</i> provide some reason for hope, <b>the first interview had the guy in charge saying that one of his bits of advice for the authors was \u201cblame the Hermetics\u201d when problematic material came up.</b> I'd much rather they <i>don't</i> try to dump everything on the Hermetics, for the same reason I prefer that the Technocracy owns its own failings and doesn't foist then off on the Nephandi. In both cases, I'm not a big fan of scapegoating. Own up to your own problems, and then move forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was <i>exactly</i> the thing that triggered this post. Fine, the Hermetics sucked in the past. But, they must also have done some good and right things, or why didn't the other Traditions hunt them all down and Gilgul them all? Why aren't they all Nephandi or Marauder?<br /> <br /> My theory is that the Order of Hermes still has the stench of the Tremere on them from White Wolf's Vampire line. And the Tremere were <i>supposed</i> to be untrustworthy assholes. But the Order of Hermes is not the Tremere, and should have done enough good things to balance out the bad stuff at the very least to still actually be part of the Council of Nine.<br /> <br /> Let all the Traditions own their own shit, and let's end the practice of sticking an entire Tradition with the Hat of Assery. That's what the Nephandi are for. Occasionally, the Marauders as well. If the Traditions fuck up, let it be bad/wrong individuals who need to get corrected by good/right individuals, preferably the player-characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 01-30-2022, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T18:44:52-08:00","id":1473620,"title":"","content":"There is a lot in their philosophy to with isolation from others in pursuit of enlightenment. They could not have been patrolling the other Traditions, enforcing their will, if they spent significant time in Hermetic Isolation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T02:08:02-08:00","id":1473637,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the first interview was citing \u201cblame the Hermetics\u201d in the context of how utterly screwed up some of the existing nomenclature in Mage is, specifically things like Tradition names and Traditionist names (e.g., the Akashic Brotherhood and Battering Ram). It appears that the writer of the Akashayana chapter didn't follow this suggestion, for which I'm thankful. <br /> <br /> Similarly, the Dreamspeakers chapter makes a point that the other Traditions haven't exactly treated them well in the past; but it doesn't single out the Hermetics was being particularly bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T04:36:37-08:00","id":1473639,"title":"","content":"When I run I tend the emphasise a realpolitik aspects of dreamspeakers formation its not implausible that disenfranchised shamanic people would anticipate the need for a big tent movement considering time is a sphere. <br /> <br /> Then again I tend to run tengrinism, lithuanian paganism and shinto as a prominent groups in sect to flesh then out a bit more and intersectional thinking is quite popular.<br /> <br /> I don't like blame order of Hermes for everything for a number of reasons. Not in the least because its makes the wizard classic option a bit too diet tremere. But also tends to whitewash other traditions shortcomings a little<br /> For example I made it clear the euro centric verbenna, isolationist tafitani and snobby euthanatos were also partly to blame for declining to create a unified polytheist alliance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-31-2022, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T05:00:00-08:00","id":1473640,"title":"","content":"While each of the factions have their shortcomings and &quot;skeletons in the closet&quot;, the whole blame the Order of Hermes thing probably stems from the fact that the Order of Hermes have always been a bunch of arrogant, selfish, and power hungry (and a little racist) wizards since the dark ages. While they have gotten better since the departure of the Tremere, they can still get into some trouble because of their diverse paradigm emphasizing their general desire to become gods.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that the Order of Reason and subsequently the Technocracy was formed indirectly due to the bad apples of the Order of Hermes enslaving innocent villagers for their own ends and using magic for very selfish reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 01-31-2022, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T06:12:43-08:00","id":1473645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473640#post1473640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While each of the factions have their shortcomings and &quot;skeletons in the closet&quot;, the whole blame the Order of Hermes thing probably stems from the fact that the Order of Hermes have always been a bunch of arrogant, selfish, and power hungry (and a little racist) wizards since the dark ages. While they have gotten better since the departure of the Tremere, they can still get into some trouble because of their diverse paradigm emphasizing their general desire to become gods.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that the Order of Reason and subsequently the Technocracy was formed indirectly due to the bad apples of the Order of Hermes enslaving innocent villagers for their own ends and using magic for very selfish reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire Ascension war could be seen as the result of The Order of Hermes callousness, and honestly, I don't really believe they have changed that much. Then again, is it really that strange with their paradigm? It practically demands to be arrogant and condescending. As long as they believe themselves smarter than anyone else, they will keep making the same mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T06:46:01-08:00","id":1473648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473645#post1473645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The entire Ascension war could be seen as the result of The Order of Hermes callousness, and honestly, I don't really believe they have changed that much. Then again, is it really that strange with their paradigm? It practically demands to be arrogant and condescending. As long as they believe themselves smarter than anyone else, they will keep making the same mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My argument is: That has been demonstrated numerous times, to the point of being beaten to death. If the Order wasn't demonstrably capable of learning, I ague that they'd all be wiped out by now. so surely there's <i>something</i> they do right, <i>something</i> that keeps them being regarded as allies that can be trusted, <i>something</i> that keeps their members proud and loyal. I'd like to see what that something is, for a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T07:29:00-08:00","id":1473652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473648#post1473648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My argument is: That has been demonstrated numerous times, to the point of being beaten to death. If the Order wasn't demonstrably capable of learning, I ague that they'd all be wiped out by now. so surely there's <i>something</i> they do right, <i>something</i> that keeps them being regarded as allies that can be trusted, <i>something</i> that keeps their members proud and loyal. I'd like to see what that something is, for a change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A number of Traditions have an imposed problem like this. For some reason they keep making the same mistakes despite there being no specific reason that they would. The Order in particular has it bad because their imposed problems run completely counter to their paradigm. The faction that praises confidence, will, and wisdom should only risk falling to arrogance. It should be a cautionary tale, not the default state of affairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T08:28:42-08:00","id":1473666,"title":"","content":"However, a key element of Lore of the Traditions, as outlined in Chapter One, is \u201crecognizing your faults and moving to correct them\u201d. If ever there's a book to address the faults of the Order of Hermes and have them try to do better, this is it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T10:22:01-08:00","id":1473682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473666#post1473666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a key element of Lore of the Traditions, as outlined in Chapter One, is \u201crecognizing your faults and moving to correct them\u201d. If ever there's a book to address the faults of the Order of Hermes and have them try to do better, this is it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> HEAR, HEAR! And to add to that: If it's not addressed in Lore of the Traditions, make it a mission statement going forward that each group needs both it's faults <i>and</i> its saving graces discussed at some point. People playing this game need to know how a Tradition can break bad, but also what they do right and/or what saves them from collapsing. Let's not have just one Tradition carry the Hat of Assery from this point forward!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T13:59:19-08:00","id":1473694,"title":"","content":"It is similar to VTM. The Tremere are the scapegoat equivalents for the Hermetics and all of the clans blames them for a lot of things or believe they had a hand in it. But no clan, save for the Children of Osiris, have their hands clean and are blameless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T04:09:06-08:00","id":1473742,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, I find it hard to believe they have changed, but I really hope they will. Their section is the one I'm most eager to read, I want to see how the authors are going to give them a path towards redemption, or at least some much-needed self-reflection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T04:45:47-08:00","id":1473745,"title":"","content":"We'll be seeing the preview for the Order of Hermes on Friday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T06:18:39-08:00","id":1473748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473742#post1473742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, I find it hard to believe they have changed, but I really hope they will. Their section is the one I'm most eager to read, I want to see how the authors are going to give them a path towards redemption, or at least some much-needed self-reflection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a big part of fixing them is humility. Not a false or fawning humility that in which they've &quot;learned the error of imposing their will&quot; or something like that. It wouldn't fix the Hermetics to take away their imposing will or their sense of purpose because that is part of who they are. Instead they need a true humility that tempers their deserved confidence and keeps it from tipping into arrogance. <br /> <br /> I don't think this is a change in the faction so much as a change in the writing. Simply making it clear that they know the path they walk risks tipping them over into hubris would go a long way towards establishing the distinction between confidence and arrogance. That and a moratorium on writing any more arrogance induced mistakes for them would, I think, do most of the rehabilitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T09:44:45-08:00","id":1473756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473507#post1473507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But obviously any Muslim or Hindu Chorister etc hardline septarian didn\u2019t go Templar, so where are they? New Crafts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would there really be that many that would need to leave? In general Islam shares a lot of the same philosophies as Christianity (including worshiping the same monotheistic god), and while Hinduism is polytheistic on the surface it tends to feature concepts such as The One being manifest through the various deities of different sects. I'd think that people who were hardliners about their specific religion's dogma rather than accepting of a syncretic meta-religion would never have joined the Celestial Chorus in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T11:59:30-08:00","id":1473765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473756#post1473756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would there really be that many that would need to leave? In general Islam shares a lot of the same philosophies as Christianity (including worshiping the same monotheistic god), and while Hinduism is polytheistic on the surface it tends to feature concepts such as The One being manifest through the various deities of different sects. I'd think that people who were hardliners about their specific religion's dogma rather than accepting of a syncretic meta-religion would never have joined the Celestial Chorus in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chorus though has been portrayed having heavy sectarian Christian factions in the past, one\u2019s that were even in power during the imperial missionary era as shown in the Victorian Mage manuscript.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T05:14:35-08:00","id":1473816,"title":"","content":"That's one of the bigger problems with the Chorus, writing-wise. They are trying to have it both ways. They are both the default faction for Christian, Muslim, and other monotheistic mages, and a secret organization that is explicitly not Christian or Muslim or any other extant religion (a fictional, millenia-old Theosophical Society). <br /> <br /> It makes sense that they should be the former (at least by now, if not at the forming of the Traditions), but their splat is written like they are the latter. And indeed if they are the latter, there should be some place in the Traditions where the dissenters go. Rejecting the philosophies of the Chorus is not the same thing as rejecting membership in the Traditions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T06:27:59-08:00","id":1473821,"title":"","content":"I don't see why the \u201cplace to go\u201d needs to be in the Traditions: <br /> <br /> \u2022 The Templars seem to be a near-perfect fit for sectarian Christians; and to the extent that it doesn't, I could see the influx of defectors from the Celestial Chorus changing it so that it does. <br /> \u2022 Sectarian Muslims fit in the Ahl-i-Batin, last I checked; though I could be wrong about that. <br /> \u2022 Sectarian Jews pose a unique problem, in that a faction of secret Jewish mystics operating behind the scenes has some very uncomfortable parallels to real-world antisemitic conspiracy theories; I'm guessing that's why absolutely no effort has been made by anyone to even acknowledge the Lions of Zion that were presented in the Sorcerers Crusade Companion, let alone update them for the modern world. <br /> \u2022 And other sectarian monotheists don't strike me as being plentiful enough to warrant dedicated Crafts \u2014 though I'm willing to be persuaded otherwise. For the most part, the \u201cnew homes\u201d for non-Abrahamic former Choristers who abandoned the Tradition because of the new Doctrine of Comity (paraphrasing, \u201cyour religious convictions come second to the goal of harmony\u201d) are groups that have other interests as their primary focus: the manuscript suggests that the departing Choristers ended up going to the likes of \u201cthe Order of Hermes, Children of Knowledge, Ngoma, Society of Ether, Verbena, Akashayana, or paradigmatically appropriate groups\u201d. <br /> <br /> Also, a pseudo-Theosophic group with Christian trappings seems to fit the Traditions quite well, given their overall philosophy of \u201cwe're all doing the same thing, just with different trappings\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T06:41:56-08:00","id":1473822,"title":"","content":"I indeed assume any disgruntled Jewish mage or sorcerer with the Chorus would jump ship to the Lions of Zion or Mogen HaChav.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T07:24:07-08:00","id":1473825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473821#post1473821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why the \u201cplace to go\u201d needs to be in the Traditions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Templars seem to be a near-perfect fit for sectarian Christians; and to the extent that it doesn't, I could see the influx of defectors from the Celestial Chorus changing it so that it does.<br /> \u2022 Sectarian Muslims fit in the Ahl-i-Batin, last I checked; though I could be wrong about that.<br /> \u2022 Sectarian Jews pose a unique problem, in that a faction of secret Jewish mystics operating behind the scenes has some very uncomfortable parallels to real-world antisemitic conspiracy theories; I'm guessing that's why absolutely no effort has been made by anyone to even acknowledge the Lions of Zion that were presented in the Sorcerers Crusade Companion, let alone update them for the modern world.<br /> \u2022 And other sectarian monotheists don't strike me as being plentiful enough to warrant dedicated Crafts \u2014 though I'm willing to be persuaded otherwise. For the most part, the \u201cnew homes\u201d for non-Abrahamic former Choristers who abandoned the Tradition because of the new Doctrine of Comity (paraphrasing, \u201cyour religious convictions come second to the goal of harmony\u201d) are groups that have other interests as their primary focus: the manuscript suggests that the departing Choristers ended up going to the likes of \u201cthe Order of Hermes, Children of Knowledge, Ngoma, Society of Ether, Verbena, Akashayana, or paradigmatically appropriate groups\u201d.<br /> <br /> Also, a pseudo-Theosophic group with Christian trappings seems to fit the Traditions quite well, given their overall philosophy of \u201cwe're all doing the same thing, just with different trappings\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't need to be, but why should leaving the Chorus mean leaving the Traditions? I agree with you that pseudo-Theosophists are a good fit for the Traditions, but so are a lot of mages with fundamentalist (as opposed to extremist) religious beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T13:53:17-08:00","id":1473993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1473821#post1473821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why the \u201cplace to go\u201d needs to be in the Traditions:<br /> \u2022 Sectarian Muslims fit in the Ahl-i-Batin, last I checked; though I could be wrong about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're Sufi or Ismai'li, yes definitely. More mainstream Sunni and DEFINITELY Salafi Muslims are going to be uncomfortable though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T08:48:04-08:00","id":1474286,"title":"","content":"So, kind of feels like they are a bit heavy handed with the 'Europeans did bad bad things' message maybe? Especially after seeing them not go into any detail on the things the Chinese government has done when they mention 'oh, and the Akashayana joined the CPC but they totally just wanted to help people from the inside so aiding it was cool'. And I don't mean that they shouldn't have mentioned it at all, I seriously just think they should be a bit more even handed and call out terrible non-Europeans as well. Europeans didn't have a copyright on being awful people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-09-2022, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T10:37:10-08:00","id":1474299,"title":"","content":"They <i>did</i> seem to be laying it on a bit thick in the Etherite chapter. But to be fair, the Etherites <i>do</i> have a history of being an \u201cold boys club\u201d and, to a lesser extent, favoring Europeans; so some attention to it is warranted there. <br /> <br /> But yeah: on the one hand, it's a thing; but on the other hand, Western culture in the book as a whole is coming across as \u201cthe devil incarnate\u201d, which perhaps swings the pendulum a bit too far the other way. And yes, part of that is that other cultures (such as the Chinese) aren't getting called out to anywhere near the same extent that the West is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T10:57:55-08:00","id":1474303,"title":"","content":"Circling back to the Akashayana, they kind of didn't feel like they fit in with the theme of the traditions having to undergo some deep difficult introspection and make changes to keep up with a changing world in general. &quot;Yeah we absorbed the Wulong but that has been going great aside from temporarily annoying a few bureaucrats in the Shi-Ren' and 'some members aren't super keen on this internet thing but aren't causing problems for the people that are' seemed to be the closest they had to faction conflict in how it would act going forward. They pretty much just go 'we have been getting it right for 3 thousand years and will continue to get it right with only superficial changes like now having skype to communicate with instead of needing to use magic' and more or less brush off the loss of Horizon and the avatar storm as a generic weakening that lead to them assimilating some crafts with no serious difficulty of integration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-09-2022, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T13:18:06-08:00","id":1474320,"title":"","content":"Like the Dreamspeakers better, they do have the same 'we never did anything wrong' thing going on but as less a coherent faction and more a bunch of different factions crammed together by politics they don't really have much of a central coherent history to speak of that they could use to do bad things. Though there are a couple of weird parts where they do this weird thing where they say 'we didn't have a choice in joining/only joined because it was in our best interests against outside pressure' that made me go &quot;....Yes? That is all the traditions, all of you only joined together because of outside pressure from the technocrats making you desperate enough to pool your resources together with people you normally wanted nothing to do with against a common enemy. Nobody made you show up to the Conclave and nobody is stopping you from leaving like plenty of others have left after joining so what is this talk about being dragged into the organization against your will and it being 'their war'?&quot;.<br /> <br /> They also have kept to the theme and gave plenty of hooks about how they are struggling on the new direction, have naysayers that are digging in their heels even on matters where it seems like changes have been decided to go, and going into detail on how it has brutalized them to lose so many strongholds to things like the avatar storm because many of those places held often irreplaceable cultural and magical knowledge so screw those guys that say 'well, in the end, it was totally for the best because we need to focus on Earth anyway instead of secluding ourselves in magic land'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-09-2022, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T15:38:17-08:00","id":1474332,"title":"","content":"Celestial chorus seems to do a pretty good job of getting across how bad it has messed up previously without getting heavy handed about it. It is interesting to see a mage created Unitarian religion that tries to convince other religions that their religion is just a facet giving them a glimpse at the one true religion and the One being. And of course they definitely match up with the idea of reforming the Traditions to fix past issues what with them basically rebuilding the Chorus from the ground up and seeing a bunch of their dudes leave while getting an influx of newcomers from many disparate religious backgrounds that leaves its ultimate state once it settles in flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T17:45:34-08:00","id":1474931,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading the manuscript. Lots of good thing. With the exception of the etherite part which is at best pretty meh.<br /> <br /> Now for the ugly detail. *Sigh*<br /> <br /> Who amongs the writters (I have my idea) though making Elon Musk a villain (or even nephandic) Son of ether was a good idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T17:52:59