aditions-is-here?p=1474933#post1474933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must agree. Elon is a wonderful man,he has helped a lof of people. Made the world a better place. He's a hero,through and through.<br /> the writer is just jealous</div> </div> </div> </div>What about what he did to his son.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T18:01:04-08:00","id":1474935,"title":"","content":"Eh. It was just a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T18:07:03-08:00","id":1474938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1474935#post1474935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. It was just a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing some of the writers, not sure of that.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's hypocritical when WW constantly says they no longuer make historical or contenporary figures parts of the supernatural communities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T18:15:56-08:00","id":1474939,"title":"","content":"The Sons of Ether chapter is definitely heavily politically biased; so the Elon Musk reference doesn't surprise me. I don't expect the slanting to be corrected, though \u2014 I suspect that the author probably doesn't even think it <i>is</i> slanted. So I'll just invoke the \u201cunreliable narrator\u201d trope and make the best of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T06:03:22-08:00","id":1475036,"title":"","content":"For someone who hasn't backed, what kind of quackery plagues the Etherite chapter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T09:11:23-08:00","id":1475043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1474933#post1474933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must agree. Elon is a wonderful man,he has helped a lof of people. Made the world a better place. He's a hero,through and through.<br /> the writer is just jealous</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elon Musk who made anti union statement who also recently tweeted a picture of Hitler comparing it to Canadian prime minister Justin Trudeau in which he recently deleted without any apology or statement?<br /> <br /> Funny enough on a discord chat someone disliked the new sub faction of the virtual adapts called the mercurial elites because he described them as the type of tech bros who would idolize people like Elon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 02-20-2022, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T18:58:16-08:00","id":1475075,"title":"","content":"I hate Elon Musk, but making him a villain, especially if objectively true in the setting, is a bad decision if done without his consent, because this is still slanting against a living person. The fictional nature of the slant can be taken in several ways, but I'm personally against using it as justification.<br /> <br /> There are better ways to criticize someone directly in your works without resorting to such tactics. Some SoE could discuss Elon's works directly and by name and drop their opinions, both political and on how it affects their magic. That would be direct, avoid fictional slander, and make the point over concrete facts as concrete facts and subjective opinions as subjective opinions.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: I may be wrong, but wasn't <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24222_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24222\" data-vbnamecard=\"24222\">Acopiltaczet</a> just being sarcastic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T02:43:55-08:00","id":1475095,"title":"","content":"I grabbed the Etherite chapter, and couldn't find any reference for 'Elon' or 'Musk', so...whaaat is this about...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T07:00:33-08:00","id":1475104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then there\u2019s that fucking tech billionaire, like so many others. A failed or fallen student of the Kitab al-Alacir lost to his own depravity, fucker had the audacity to acquire an energies company named for an Etherite, bastardizing that legacy by affiliating with human-traffickers catering to the wealthiest echelons. </div> </div> </div>This is what they are talking about, I think? But its generic enough that I don't consider it a problem, it could easily be a fictional character in setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T08:26:22-08:00","id":1475107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475095#post1475095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I grabbed the Etherite chapter, and couldn't find any reference for 'Elon' or 'Musk', so...whaaat is this about...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, just giving my opinion, I didn't read it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475104#post1475104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what they are talking about, I think? But its generic enough that I don't consider it a problem, it could easily be a fictional character in setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually I would agree, but the complete &quot;<i>energies company named for an Etherite</i>&quot; sentence is too much on the nose for my comfort. It is too obvious to not be taken as anything but Tesla. If at least the '<i>energies'</i> bit were taken out I would agree that it is generic enough. A Tech company, or a company focused on R&amp;D, even a Manufacture, but both Energy and Car Manufacture are too narrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T08:29:19-08:00","id":1475108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475036#post1475036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For someone who hasn't backed, what kind of quackery plagues the Etherite chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to re-read the chapter to give you the most accurate answer.<br /> <br /> First, to give you an idea of how a chapter of this book is structured, you have four parts; history, current day events, three exemplen of npcs and a final part mentioning the allies of the traditions amongs other mages' factions or even nightfolks.<br /> <br /> The history, individuals and allies parts of that chapter are good. The real issue lies within the current events part.<br /> <br /> I can resume my problem with it with three issues.<br /> <br /> 1/ verbose diarrhea<br /> While the rest of the book is, to be fair, well balanced between fluff and precision, this part isn't. <br /> It really feels like someone forgot to watch over brucato here.<br /> <br /> 2/the before mentioned characterisation of Musk<br /> While he is not named, come on, the paragraph speak of him only. It's a childish attack from the authors. Same authors who constantly gloat on their supposetly acquired maturity.<br /> <br /> And the best for the end<br /> 3/american left wing politics. <br /> The grand result of infusing Science in academia is &quot;decolonial&quot; research, the evil that the etherite must fight are the &quot;edgelords&quot; of fandoms and the fascism of children in cages, etc...<br /> <br /> In advance for those that will answer that part, I know, I know, WW was always left leaning in it's views and writing.<br /> <br /> But there's a limit between having a side and shoving irrelevant political buzzwords and boggeymen in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T08:33:12-08:00","id":1475109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475104#post1475104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what they are talking about, I think? But its generic enough that I don't consider it a problem, it could easily be a fictional character in setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's extremely specific on the contrary.<br /> <br /> Do you know many &quot;fucking tech billionaire&quot; owning a company named after an etherite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T08:48:24-08:00","id":1475110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475109#post1475109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's extremely specific on the contrary.<br /> <br /> Do you know many &quot;fucking tech billionaire&quot; owning a company named after an etherite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the real Elon Musk a student of something called the Kitab al-Alacir? Enough leeway is there that it could easily be a completely fictional individual instead of a fictional mage version of a real individual.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T09:11:24-08:00","id":1475114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475110#post1475110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the real Elon Musk a student of something called the Kitab al-Alacir? Enough leeway is there that it could easily be a completely fictional individual instead of a fictional mage version of a real individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real Tesla wasn't either. Yet he is made an etherite in the game's lore.<br /> <br /> That's the point of adapting real world persons to fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T09:41:03-08:00","id":1475116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475104#post1475104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kind of feels like they are a bit heavy handed with the 'Europeans did bad bad things' message maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1474939#post1474939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on the one hand, it's a thing; but on the other hand, Western culture in the book as a whole is coming across as \u201cthe devil incarnate\u201d, which perhaps swings the pendulum a bit too far the other way. And yes, part of that is that other cultures (such as the Chinese) aren't getting called out to anywhere near the same extent that the West is.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a sign of the times. I think the people who write these books are vastly more self-aware of their implicit biases than their predecessors might have been, and are clearly sensitive to the way in which past materials might have been offensive to non-Americans and non-Westerners. I'm not going to bemoan any of that; writers in particular should be conscious of 'where they're coming from'. However, these books and writings cannot help but be the product of the minds and imaginations of people living in a particular time and place, which basically means that the <i>de rigueur</i> social politics of liberal-arts-college-educated people living in Western liberal democracies (and the United States in particular,) are necessarily the social politics of the game. Practically speaking that means a high degree of self-consciousness regarding absolutely anything that could even remotely or arguably be called colonialist (original recipe, or &quot;post-&quot;); a strong emphasis on consent (so strong in fact that the game's mechanics were altered to make mind control vastly more difficult); a desire to be seen as going out of one's way to be deferential and accommodating to &quot;marginalized groups&quot; (in quotes because I don't think there's a consensus <i>yet</i> as to what exactly the term means or when it's appropriate); a concern with ensuring that whatever writer has the proper 'license' to write about or make characterizations about a given culture; and, with regard to writers who have working on these books since the older editions, the imperative (both on <i>and off</i> the page) to perform some shame and contrition for their participation in the creation of materials now considered insensitive, tone deaf, appropriative, what-have-you.<br /> <br /> Substantively speaking, I don't necessarily have a problem with any of this--I am one of those Western liberal arts people, and these are more or less my politics--but, unfortunately, it is a socio-political climate that favors <b>overcorrection</b>, considering that that trespasses carry strongly social penalties and stigma (and 'good faith' is not an excuse,) and what is considered verboten is in a constant-enough state of flux that I think writers and content-creators have some concerns over whether something well-received today will become an actionable item two, three, or ten years later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1474939#post1474939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sons of Ether chapter is definitely heavily politically biased; so the Elon Musk reference doesn't surprise me. I don't expect the slanting to be corrected, though \u2014 I suspect that the author probably doesn't even think it <i>is</i> slanted. So I'll just invoke the \u201cunreliable narrator\u201d trope and make the best of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> The particular flavor of political bias or &quot;slant&quot; you identify in this chapter is part and parcel of what I described above, and something I've picked up on in a few M20 release, particularly (and most recently) in &quot;Rich Bastard's Guide&quot;. Frankly, it is what it is: public opinion within certain circleshas turned strongly against capitalism, so that's going to come through. The only thing that worries me (and I hope I'm just reading too far into the tone/tenor of some of the writing,) is that tech billionaires, industrialists, or just <i>capitalists</i> writ large will become the game's new vaudevillian bad guys--complete with mustache-twirling, tying union organizers to train tracks, and goofy doomsday devices. It's not that this is offensive (to me at least, there might be some capitalism stans out there that are totally incensed,) so much as I liked the idea of moving away from uncomplicated Saturday morning cartoon villainy. I honestly don't think we're quite there yet, but we could certainly overcorrect our way there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475104#post1475104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what they are talking about, I think? But its generic enough that I don't consider it a problem, it could easily be a fictional character in setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's probably not actionable, and if they were to someday put a name to the character being referenced, I assume it would be a character that is basically Elon Musk with the serial numbers filed off (&quot;Emon Lusk&quot;? &quot;Mulon Esk&quot;?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:17:02-08:00","id":1475130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475108#post1475108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3/american left wing politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only partially agree here, given the aforementioned fact that WoD <b>is</b> political and left-wing. Never was something else nor pretended to be.<br /> <br /> But I understand your dislike. I would put it into other terms, though, there are unfortunately also very much traditional WoD. First, it is a lot of buzzwords with little examination on the actual matters at hand, at least as it seems to be (again, didn't read it myself). Second, it is distinctly <i>American</i>. Not that it can't also be American, mind you, but it is the same old PoV of white, middle-class, Democrat America instead of presenting the actual PoVs of people involved in the matter or something.<br /> <br /> A problem that has diminished, actually, but more because White Middle-Class America has improved, not because WoD has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475110#post1475110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the real Elon Musk a student of something called the Kitab al-Alacir? Enough leeway is there that it could easily be a completely fictional individual instead of a fictional mage version of a real individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the Kitab is <b><i>the canonical in-setting foundational text of the Etherites</i></b>, so no one IRL actually ever studied it, but it is a setting fact regardless.<br /> <br /> That said, seriously, there's not enough leeway. Musk is <b><u>the</u></b> tech billionaire that looks like an Etherite instead of an Adept, acquired an energies company named after someone fairly well-known that is a known Etherite in-setting, and has that much bad blood about him. In no uncertain terms this is referring to Elon Musk, it <b><u>is</u></b> a fictional mage version of a real individual, period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475116#post1475116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which basically means that the <i>de rigueur</i> social politics of liberal-arts-college-educated people living in Western liberal democracies (and the United States in particular,) are necessarily the social politics of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally have a strong dislike for the notion of &quot;Western Liberal Democracies&quot;, because it ignores a lot of nuance between countries both in and outside that &quot;group&quot;. But more importantly and deriving from this, the American left is actually far more specific in its culture and ideas than they think.<br /> <br /> Not that most of those things aren't common to the left across the globe, but there are a lot of specifics that greatly affect how WoD is written and are quite American.<br /> <br /> On top of that, AFAIK even defining those leanings as &quot;liberal&quot; is a very American thing to do, because this label has other connotations elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475116#post1475116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that worries me (and I hope I'm just reading too far into the tone/tenor of some of the writing,) is that tech billionaires, industrialists, or just <i>capitalists</i> writ large will become the game's new vaudevillian bad guys--complete with mustache-twirling, tying union organizers to train tracks, and goofy doomsday devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to make it clear, some of those guys fully deserve the treatment, and while I don't think it right to do it in the book as it was done, Elon Musk is definitely one of them. Steve Jobs was another. I otherwise agree that going so far across the board wouldn't be desirable or fair, but the case in hand is very specific and warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:32:40-08:00","id":1475132,"title":"","content":"If they are using the Jeffrey Epstein Scandal to impugn Elon Musk, do they say anything meaningful about the former?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T12:59:38-08:00","id":1475141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475130#post1475130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally have a strong dislike for the notion of &quot;Western Liberal Democracies&quot;, because it ignores a lot of nuance between countries both in and outside that &quot;group&quot;. But more importantly and deriving from this, the American left is actually far more specific in its culture and ideas than they think.<br /> <br /> Not that most of those things aren't common to the left across the globe, but there are a lot of specifics that greatly affect how WoD is written and are quite American.</div> </div> </div> </div> I could probably have just called it &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberal_democracy\" target=\"_blank\">liberal democracy</a>&quot;, but what I was going for seemed more accurately described with the word &quot;Western&quot; tacked on to the front; for the purposes of my description, I necessarily wanted to include the aesthetics, trappings, and (for lack of a better term,) &quot;baggage&quot; that comes part and parcel with being a person whose cultural traditions and sense of identity is very strongly (or perhaps even solely) informed by so-called &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_culture\" target=\"_blank\">western civilization</a>.&quot; In other words, it's not just about higher ideals and nominal notions of what is good and desirable, or what constitutes fairness and justice--it's very much also about the set of stories and history that one believes they have a right to claim, and maybe more important than that, the hagiography one feels a responsibility, or even <i>duty,</i> to push back against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475130#post1475130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, AFAIK even defining those leanings as &quot;liberal&quot; is a very American thing to do, because this label has other connotations elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with you. I used the term in this context despite the limited mileage it might have outside the U.S. or Canada, because the people writing these books, inclusive of &quot;Lore of the Traditions&quot;, are Americans, or at least <i>North American</i>, living and writing in North America if not the U.S. itself. So while I agree that my usage of the word &quot;liberal&quot; is pretty specialized (and I acknowledge that there isn't even widespread agreement within the weeds of modern American political discourse as to <i>what</i> it means to be &quot;a liberal&quot;,) I'll stand by this use-case scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475130#post1475130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make it clear, some of those guys fully deserve the treatment, and while I don't think it right to do it in the book as it was done, Elon Musk is definitely one of them. Steve Jobs was another. I otherwise agree that going so far across the board wouldn't be desirable or fair, but the case in hand is very specific and warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think we're of a mind on this. For me it's not about whether this class of person <i>deserves</i> to be depicted in any particular way; it's about whether I want (I'll refer back to my own description) &quot;uncomplicated Saturday morning cartoon villainy&quot; in the first place. M20 gave us an entire book that serves (at least partially,) as a fairly nuanced metaphysical/cosmological meditation on evil; turning around and depicting a crude facsimile of the odious tech billionaire <i>du juour,</i> as a Captain Planet villain, or a parody of a James Bond villain, would feel cheap and more than a little goofy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T13:06:33-08:00","id":1475142,"title":"","content":"I actually kind of don't mind the Elon Musk reference, other than the implication that there appears to be a sharp divide between the \u201cGood Etherites\u201d who have embraced the aforementioned American left-wing agenda and the \u201cBad Etherites\u201d who haven't. I could see throwing a Steve Jobs for Elon Musk expie into the Dissidents faction \u2014 those Etherites who object to the Tradition imposing a uniform code of ethics on all members \u2014 but the book carries the implication that if you're not on board with the new standards of decency that the Tradition is apparently now pushing, you're probably Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T14:10:27-08:00","id":1475146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475132#post1475132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are using the Jeffrey Epstein Scandal to impugn Elon Musk, do they say anything meaningful about the former?</div> </div> </div> </div> What I find ironic about this is that, despite Epstein having been an uncontroversially reviled sort of &quot;evil&quot; person, he might be less likely to be parodied or used as inspiration for fictional villains engaged in sinister plots and conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The reason I find this ironic is because, generally speaking, human traffickers (and child sex traffickers in particular,) are probably last kind of law breaker or criminal that Hollywood protagonists can categorically brutalized with total moral impunity; you don't need to know about how they do business, or why they do what they do--the fact alone that they're engaged in trafficking (**without themselves being a trafficked person**) automatically makes them utterly unsympathetic and worthy of summary execution by any means and by <i>whomever</i>. Tack on the fact that the man was a fabulously wealthy elite who literally conspired to with other rich elites to engage in evil conduct, and you really can't get more odious. So by all rights, this guy's fictional stand-ins and alter-egos should be burned in effigy <i>ad infinitum </i>throughout movies and TV... but I don't think he is. My hypothesis as to why he's <i>not </i>is two-fold: first, Epstein had real victims--real people who are alive, walking around, presumably still dealing with the trauma of what Epstein and his co-conspirators put them through, so when a writer creates an Epstein stand-in, they aren't just co-opting the memory and a story of Epstein, they're necessarily co-opting the stories of untold numbers of victims and survivors who may or may not appreciate or approve of a depiction that seeks to profit from their trauma.<br /> <br /> The second reason I don't think Epstein-stand-in villains are going to come to prominence any time soon is that Epstein is already the central figure in untold numbers of conspiracy theories promulgated by the American far right, Qanoners, and assorted other &quot;rugged individualist free thinkers&quot;; conspiracy theories with such a huge range, that they can go from the <i>relatively</i> mundane, all the way up to <i>lizard people drinking children's eye juice in order to power their satanic rituals</i> (which already sounds like it was lifted from Mage 2ed.,) So of course anyone who puts pen to paper and writes about any remotely Epstein-like figure at the center of a conspiracy is immediately going to worry about whether they're going to be associated with a whackadoo fascist ultra-nationalist movement, or feed into that movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T14:52:26-08:00","id":1475151,"title":"","content":"What do you think of Garrick Browne (<b>Book of the Fallen</b> pp.199\u2013200)? More generally, the Mammonites are <i>all about</i> Epstein-style exploitation. <br /> <br /> That is, Epstein-style villains already exist in Mage, and they're right where they belong: among the Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T19:45:19-08:00","id":1475174,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/doggies-draculas-5e-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/doggies-dracu...meeting-notes/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, we took a look at the <b>M20 Lore of the Traditions </b>KS, which almost hit 400% funding, and overall did really well for us and started the year with a bang! We cleared enough Stretch Goals to create two new <b>M20 </b>books, which is fabulous news!<br /> In fact, we were this morning OK\u2019d by <b>Paradox </b>to create and crowdfund another <b>M20 </b>supplement, but I can\u2019t tell you our plans with that book just yet.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Nice, looks like this did well enough Paradox is up for some more M20, was worried this would be the last round of 20th anniversary content when I heard rumor they had shot down a 20th anniversary hunter book.<br /> <br /> Sad the next round of kickstarter won't be exalted, though. The wait on its splat books is killing me, lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T20:51:09-08:00","id":1475180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475146#post1475146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWhat I find ironic about this is that, despite Epstein having been an uncontroversially reviled sort of &quot;evil&quot; person, he might be less likely to be parodied or used as inspiration for fictional villains engaged in sinister plots and conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The reason I find this ironic is because, generally speaking, human traffickers (and child sex traffickers in particular,) are probably last kind of law breaker or criminal that Hollywood protagonists can categorically brutalized with total moral impunity; you don't need to know about how they do business, or why they do what they do--the fact alone that they're engaged in trafficking (**without themselves being a trafficked person**) automatically makes them utterly unsympathetic and worthy of summary execution by any means and by <i>whomever</i>. Tack on the fact that the man was a fabulously wealthy elite who literally conspired to with other rich elites to engage in evil conduct, and you really can't get more odious. So by all rights, this guy's fictional stand-ins and alter-egos should be burned in effigy <i>ad infinitum </i>throughout movies and TV... but I don't think he is. My hypothesis as to why he's <i>not </i>is two-fold: first, Epstein had real victims--real people who are alive, walking around, presumably still dealing with the trauma of what Epstein and his co-conspirators put them through, so when a writer creates an Epstein stand-in, they aren't just co-opting the memory and a story of Epstein, they're necessarily co-opting the stories of untold numbers of victims and survivors who may or may not appreciate or approve of a depiction that seeks to profit from their trauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I don't think victims' trauma should be a reason not to depict events, if the depiction would shed light on the subject and interest some portion of the audience in combatting sex trafficking. Trauma can be recovered from. If we let the Epstein thing fade into distant memory, there may be more people - I mean girls 14 to 17 - with nobody to turn to. I want to see everyone involved prosecuted and sentenced. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475146#post1475146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second reason I don't think Epstein-stand-in villains are going to come to prominence any time soon is that Epstein is already the central figure in untold numbers of conspiracy theories promulgated by the American far right, Qanoners, and assorted other &quot;rugged individualist free thinkers&quot;; conspiracy theories with such a huge range, that they can go from the <i>relatively</i> mundane, all the way up to <i>lizard people drinking children's eye juice in order to power their satanic rituals</i> (which already sounds like it was lifted from Mage 2ed.,) So of course anyone who puts pen to paper and writes about any remotely Epstein-like figure at the center of a conspiracy is immediately going to worry about whether they're going to be associated with a whackadoo fascist ultra-nationalist movement, or feed into that movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a conversation with someone recently who had believed the Reptilians conspiracy theory. They always hated the British Royal Family and had been easily convinced. The funny thing was that they did not know much about David Icke. Before presenting evidence that Icke is a lying opportunist, I went into a spiel about confirmation bias. explaining how a false belief will give you the urge to defend it, even when you are presented with proof of its falsehood. They agreed to look at the evidence I wanted to show. We watched the interview in which Icke sat in front of a live studio audience and claimed to be a prophet, everyone laughing in his face. My friend no longer believes the Queen is a lizard, but still hates the Monarchy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475151#post1475151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of Garrick Browne (<b>Book of the Fallen</b> pp.199\u2013200)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. I have a blind spot, there. Due to the strong preference of one of my players for excluding the Nephandi from the setting, I totally forgot about BOTF. <br /> <br /> Garrick Browne is based on Elon Musk. Another thing I think about that entry is that it is desperate to push the political agenda we are talking about here. After going on about how he is intent on extracting Earth to build his space base, it slides in a comment about how this Nephandi mastermind only buys out cis-gendered white men. As a member of this demographic, I would like to be able to look forward to new material without constantly being told that I'm shit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475151#post1475151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More generally, the Mammonites are <i>all about</i> Epstein-style exploitation.<br /> <br /> That is, Epstein-style villains already exist in Mage, and they're right where they belong: among the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T21:55:32-08:00","id":1475186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475146#post1475146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I find ironic about this is that, despite Epstein having been an uncontroversially reviled sort of &quot;evil&quot; person, he might be less likely to be parodied or used as inspiration for fictional villains engaged in sinister plots and conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have a simpler theory for this.<br /> <br /> For all his evil, speaking strictly from a literary perspective, Epstein is a more generic villain.<br /> <br /> Villains that do what he did already exist, and they are many (or at least as much as possible for such sensitive content). Rich guy that indulges in ultimate decadence, has good relations with other rich people, and maintains a facade through philanthropy. This is a trope more than a character, and there's little to add for him specifically. Some settings actually go as far as to assume the entirety of the upper class is like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T05:17:10-08:00","id":1475224,"title":"","content":"You know what? I'm going to suggest an edit to the Etherites chapter, to the effect that the paragraph talking about Elon Musk in all but name should be rewritten to refer to Garrick Browne. It would be kind of absurd to have <i>both</i> Musk <i>and</i> Browne in the setting, and both Awakened; and since Browne's existence in the setting has been confirmed, that's yet another reason to leave Musk out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T06:06:10-08:00","id":1475228,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that I see no need to make every relevant person into a supernatural. If it was even needed to have Musk represented in the setting, he could still be just the mundane human he is IRL, as it never stopped him in the first place.<br /> <br /> Just because the guy gloats about his technology as if he was a kind of wizard doesn't mean he has to be able to back it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T06:44:18-08:00","id":1475232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475224#post1475224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what? I'm going to suggest an edit to the Etherites chapter, to the effect that the paragraph talking about Elon Musk in all but name should be rewritten to refer to Garrick Browne.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is, that Browne is an ex-VE/NWO, not ex-Etherite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T09:10:10-08:00","id":1475236,"title":"","content":"Unaware political leanings and inconsistency about referencing public figures and organizations were present in the M20 core and they ended up being an annoying but ignorable element. It does sound like it is starting to affect setting elements here. That's not really a problem either since I can adjust that for my table. It's just the more I have to do that, the less incentive I have to pick up the book in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T10:08:14-08:00","id":1475241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475151#post1475151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of Garrick Browne (<b>Book of the Fallen</b> pp.199\u2013200)? More generally, the Mammonites are <i>all about</i> Epstein-style exploitation.<br /> <br /> That is, Epstein-style villains already exist in Mage, and they're right where they belong: among the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div> I saw Browne as more a pastiche of various hated tech billionaires, most strongly Musk and Peter Thiel, with Bezos somewhere in third place.<br /> <br /> I won't get into the Elon Musk elements because they're obvious enough that I'm arguing here that it's not <i>just</i> Musk. That said, I see <i><u>a lot</u></i> of Peter Thiel in there: Browne's moniker is &quot;The King of Investments&quot; (which is what Theil does--he invests in companies and people,) the write-up says Browne's pet projects are apps (which tracks with Thiel's history as more of a software/fintech/VC guy,) the write-up has him as practicing some regressive social politics (big ol' &quot;check&quot; for Thiel there as well if you consider his more infamous forays into electoral politics,) and there's certainly an argument to be made for the real-world Thiel being in league with all manner of malign forces--because I'm not sure what else to call people and companies whose intentional output is unchecked misinformation and human hatred. The space aspect again tracks with Musk, but also Bezos--ditto &quot;the high-profile&quot; divorces/breakups/partners.<br /> <br /> If there had specifically been mention of anti-competitive behavior, or gobbling up competitors with abandon, I would have made more of an argument for Bezos, or even Zuckerberg. With that in mind, I curiously see basically <i>zero</i> Mark Zuckerberg in there, because Browne is described as charismatic and &quot;can sway a crowd of skeptics simply by smiling on a stage[,]&quot; and that is more or less the complete opposite of Mark Zuckerberg, who I am increasingly convinced is an evil Soong-type android sent back in time from the future to foment mental illness, division, and genocide.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I get why the writers wouldn't want to collapse <i>every </i>detestable tech billionaire into a single person--you would have ended up with a single Earthly person as the causal nexus for a whole-number-percentage of human misery (writ large) in the modern world; essentially a Nephandus who bootstrapped themselves into what amounts to a Maeljin Incarna. Hey now, <i>there's </i>an idea...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475180#post1475180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, I don't think victims' trauma should be a reason not to depict events, if the depiction would shed light on the subject and interest some portion of the audience in combatting sex trafficking. Trauma can be recovered from. If we let the Epstein thing fade into distant memory, there may be more people - I mean girls 14 to 17 - with nobody to turn to. I want to see everyone involved prosecuted and sentenced.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree that a victim's trauma is not a reason to not depict events for the reasons you say, but the term &quot;depiction&quot; is <i><u>very</u> </i>broad. It would not be incongruous to take the position that, on the one hand, documentaries and journalistic reporting are effective and appropriate means of ensuring the memory of Epstein and his crimes don't fade away, maintain pressure on law enforcement to investigate and prosecute co-conspirators, and raise awareness of sex trafficking--while (on the other hand,) holding the position that fictional depictions of Epstein (or Epstein-in-all-but-name,) are inappropriate in a game book about fantasy wizards. If what you care about is people being prosecuted, awareness being raised, etc., then the non-fictional journalistic/documentarian camp has you more than covered. To be honest, I don't know where I stand on this exactly--and I'm not sure my opinion on this matter should even really count for anything here--but I can see content creators exercising restraint around this matter for the reasons I've given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475180#post1475180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a conversation with someone recently who had believed the Reptilians conspiracy theory. They always hated the British Royal Family and had been easily convinced. The funny thing was that they did not know much about David Icke. Before presenting evidence that Icke is a lying opportunist, I went into a spiel about confirmation bias. explaining how a false belief will give you the urge to defend it, even when you are presented with proof of its falsehood. They agreed to look at the evidence I wanted to show. We watched the interview in which Icke sat in front of a live studio audience and claimed to be a prophet, everyone laughing in his face. My friend no longer believes the Queen is a lizard, but still hates the Monarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div> First of all, congratulations: you not only did something very difficult (persuaded someone away from a dangerous, necessarily self-sealing conspiracy theory,) but you also might have saved this person's life, freedom, and livelihood given what these conspiracy theories can lead people to do (<i>see also </i>Pizzagate; Jan. 6 Capitol Insurrection.) Having said all that, I don't think it's wholly reasonable to expect that even half of the people bought into Q, lizard people, flat Earth, and similar theories are persuadable through evidence-based logical arguments, or reason. Human beings are excellent at rationalization in favor of their beliefs, <i>particularly </i>when those beliefs are strongly tied to their sense of identity (which is often the case with conspiracy theories since it automatically casts the believer as one of the elite/clever/select bunch of free thinkers who see <i>the truth</i>, and everyone else as a sheep or cog.) All of that to say this: saving people from themselves is great, but it's probably not as viable a long-term strategy for managing the issue as simply accepting that these sorts of people come part and parcel with living in an open society, accepting that they're probably not going anywhere, and plan accordingly (which plan may include taking steps to avoid those people, or even being tangentially associated with them.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475228#post1475228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have a simpler theory for this.<br /> <br /> For all his evil, speaking strictly from a literary perspective, Epstein is a more generic villain.<br /> <br /> Villains that do what he did already exist, and they are many (or at least as much as possible for such sensitive content). Rich guy that indulges in ultimate decadence, has good relations with other rich people, and maintains a facade through philanthropy. This is a trope more than a character, and there's little to add for him specifically. Some settings actually go as far as to assume the entirety of the upper class is like that.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this as good an explanation as what I put forward. My only rejoinder to this is that being an over-the-plate sort of trope-y bad guy doesn't seem to be dispositive of being written into these games. As an example from the present discussion, the evil wealthy industrialist is basically also a trope (e.g., Lex Luxthor; Norman Osborn; David Xanatos, though he's more <i>gray </i>I guess,) but this is nevertheless a discussion about the extent to which magical facsimiles of whatever tech billionaire have or should be written into the game as antagonists. Another example would be that of the evil charlatan church/cult/religious leader; &quot;Book of the Fallen&quot; very obviously seems to have stand-ins for the likes of Pat Robertson, Joel Osteen, <i>et. al.</i>, but there's nothing new or novel about the idea of an <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CorruptChurch\" target=\"_blank\">evil church</a> or <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CorruptChurch\" target=\"_blank\">evil religious leader</a> (<i>see </i>BoF, p. 69; &quot;The New Rite Church&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 02-22-2022, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T18:26:17-08:00","id":1475275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1472681-lore-of-traditions-is-here?p=1475241#post1475241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only rejoinder to this is that being an over-the-plate sort of trope-y bad guy doesn't seem to be dispositive of being written into these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but my point was simpler. It is less that making an Epstein facsimile would be redundant (and it would be), and more that you would hardly even notice the character as an Epstein facsimile unless too many names were dropped. If you say human sex trafficking, connections in high society and career in finances, it will still be a fairly generic character. For Musk we literally could pinpoint the guy with tech billionaire, energies company and named after an Etherite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T13:32:15-08:00","id":1475464,"title":"","content":"Just want to go on the record and say that &quot;Elon Musk is canonically a Mage in M20&quot; sounds like a poor attempt at satirizing writing on the weaker end of WoD's output.<br /> <br /> 1: it's tacky to make a living IRL celebrity into a Mage.<br /> <br /> 2: Elon Musk is not a good candidate for being a Mage. He isn't enlightened, positively or negatively, he's an apartheid heir with unethical business practices who is desperate for teenagers to think he's dope. The absolute worst case scenario would have been &quot;Elon Musk, noted tech messiah and beloved inventor of modern times&quot;, which doesn't seem to be the content. What does seem to be in the content is this idea that Elon Musk was once an Etherite, which feeds into this myth of him as a &quot;modern inventor&quot; of some sort.<br /> <br /> Just create original characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-25-2022, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}